#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# gabor_wavelet

#% text
# `gabor_wavelet(w0)` is the Gabor wavelet of frequency w0 (default 6), the complex exponential exp(i w0 t) in a Gaussian window: in frequency pi^(-1/4) exp(-(s w - w0)^2/2) for every w.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
x = n(cos(20*pi*range(0, 255)/256))

#% cell
c = continuous_wavelet_transform(x, gabor_wavelet(6), [6, 2])

#% cell
norm(inverse_continuous_wavelet_transform(c) - x) < 1e-10
#% output
#= true

